{"title":"Tibbles","markdown":{"headingText":"Tibbles","headingAttr":{"id":"","classes":["unnumbered"],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\nAll *tidyverse* packages use an special type of data structure called **tibble**, that is the next evolution of the data frames at R. \n\n**Tibbles** are similar to data frames but they have special features that make them more interesting for data analysis. \n\n**Remember!!** First all we need to load *tidyverse* package (take into account that this package will load all tidyverse packages including tibble one).\n\n```{r, echo=TRUE, message=FALSE}\n#| code-line-numbers: false\nlibrary(tidyverse)\n```\n\n\n## Data Frames vs Tibbles\n\n### Printing\n\nThis is how `iris` data set looks as a data frame object:\n\n```{r}\n#| code-line-numbers: false\nhead(iris)\n```\n\nNow we are going to convert `iris` to a tibble, we will use tidyverse function `as_tibble()`:\n\n```{r}\niris_tb <- as_tibble(iris)\nhead(iris_tb)\n```\n\nWe see that in the console...\n* output of the data frame we only get the data displayed directly and unorganized.\n* output of the tibble shows a summary of dimensions as well as a compact visualization of the columns and types of each column. \n\n### Column Names\n\nOn tibbles column names don't need to be consecutive you can have names with spaces, like this example:\n\n```{r}\ndt <- tibble(\n  p  = c(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\"),\n  x = 1:5,\n  y = 2,\n  `sum of values` = x + y # we can reference other columns\n)\ndt\n```\n\n### Selection\n\nWhen selecting and modifying values you can work the same as a data frame but consider that the output of any selection will return a data frame always...\n\n```{r}\n# first value of first column as DF\ndt[1,1]\n```\n\nIf we want to manipulate the value we will need to do a second selection\n\n```{r}\n# first value of first column\ndt[1,1][[1]]\n```\n\n\nYou need to use name selection or double selection to access the values itself.\n\n```{r}\n#| code-line-numbers: false\n# first column as vector\ndt$p\n```\n\n```{r}\n#| code-line-numbers: false\n# first column value as value\ndt[[1]][1]\n```\n\n## Creating a tibble\n\nIn case you need to create a tibble manually, you can defined it as the following example.\n\n```{r, echo=T}\ndt <- tibble(\n  p  = c(\"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\", \"E\"),\n  x = 1:5,\n  y = 2,\n  `sum of values` = x + y\n)\ndt\n```","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"knitr"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":true,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","output-file":"03_01_tibbles.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-pre